From 080bb7a7565b8b21f8b93baa9b684f1761f84062 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vitaly Lipatov <lav@etersoft.ru>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 11:41:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/36] ACPI: IORT: validate TCL USB WLAN display GPU and audio
 DMA mappings

The OEM IORT describes composite devices, whereas Linux uses separate
USB, WLAN, display, Adreno, GMU and audio consumers. Default input-ID
lookup and assigning every composite stream to each child produce
incomplete or incorrect DMA identities.

Resolve named components through ACPI ancestry and add bounded
board-specific mapping selection for USB SID 0x540, WLAN 0xc0/0xc1, DPU
0x800/0x802/0x801, separate Adreno/GMU streams and audio SID 0x1001.
Validate OEM identity, table bounds, mapping uniqueness and the intended
SMMU. Publish the fwspec cleanup declaration for failure unwind.

Preserve software-node descriptions, check names before board matching,
and require translated DMA domains for the strict display/GPU paths.
Apply the noncoherent policy to the TCL Q6ASM PCM consumer. This
establishes DMA admission and identities; device suppliers, firmware and
hardware initialization remain separate prerequisites.
---
